  "description": "The new Routt is our large-format gravel bike, designed around a 50mm tire with clearance from 45mm to 57mm. It’s made for fast gravel that doesn’t always stay smooth. The larger tire format lets you run lower pressures for more grip and control over broken surfaces, helping the bike carry speed and stay composed when things get rough. At the same time, the Routt keeps the quick, direct feel that has always made it a gravel bike first.\nFrom a light race build to a wide-range mullet setup, the Routt can be built toward different ends of gravel without becoming overly specialized. A 3D-printed chainstay yoke creates room for the bigger tire format and up to a 48T 1x chainring, while a redesigned Moots carbon fork brings fully integrated brake routing through our Ti stem. In-house machined UDH dropouts round out a platform built for current gravel drivetrains and the roads they’re being ridden on.\nStill a Routt, built for more of what gravel has become.",
